# This is an extension of the module.list file specially for Agama.

# keep the nvmem drivers (https://bugzilla.suse.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1243350)
kernel/drivers/nvmem/
kernel/drivers/dma/fsl-edma.ko

# The naive "kernel/sound/" wildcard pulled in ~50 MiB, almost entirely
# because it kept kernel/sound/soc/ (Intel/AMD SOF DSP audio), which in turn
# makes image-janitor's firmware cleanup keep the SOF firmware/topology
# blobs under /lib/firmware/intel/sof* (~49 MiB on its own). The list below
# is a deliberately narrow selection instead: it covers the hardware most
# installs will actually hit (onboard HDA audio, USB audio, and VM virtio
# audio for openQA/VM testing) without the SOF firmware tax. Modern
# SOF-only laptops (no legacy HDA codec) and most legacy/pro-audio PCI and
# FireWire cards are intentionally left unsupported here.

# ALSA core infrastructure (snd.ko, snd-pcm, snd-timer, snd-rawmidi, ...).
# Mandatory foundation: nothing else under kernel/sound/ works without it.
kernel/sound/core/
# Legacy OSS emulation layer, not used by Orca/speech-dispatcher (ALSA/
# PulseAudio only), so drop it.
-kernel/sound/core/oss/
# MIDI sequencer core, irrelevant for speech output.
-kernel/sound/core/seq/

# Intel HD Audio (HDA) controller and per-vendor codec drivers (Realtek,
# Conexant, Cirrus, IDT, VIA, HDMI, ...). This is the dominant onboard
# audio interface on desktops/laptops since ~2005, so it covers most real
# hardware this image will be installed on.
kernel/sound/hda/

# USB Audio Class driver (snd-usb-audio) plus a few vendor USB audio
# devices. Small, but covers virtually all USB headsets/speakers/dongles
# and docks, including laptops with no onboard audio jack.
kernel/sound/usb/

# virtio-snd, the paravirtualized sound device exposed by QEMU/KVM. Needed
# for sound in VM installs and for openQA testing.
kernel/sound/virtio/
